        <OtherAbstract Type="PIP" Language="eng">
            <AbstractText>127 fertile women fitted with Lippes Loop for different periods were divided into 3 groups in order to study possible endometrial histopathological changes. Group 1, the histopathological study, contained both women who had used the IUD for less than 1 year and those who had used it for 1-10 years. In this group, endometrial histopathology and vaginal cytology were recorded upon IUD removal and followed up regularly. Group 2, the restoration of fertility study, was also divided into women with short-term IUD use (less than 1 year) and women with long-term use</AbstractText>
        </OtherAbstract>
